{"name":"Timothy Grass","hex":"#adb274","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"timothy grass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant, Phleum pratense"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/timothy_grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Timothy (grass)","blocks":[{"text":"Timothy is a species of perennial grass native to most of Europe and northern and western Asia. It is also known as timothy-grass, meadow cat's-tail or common cat's-tail. It is a member of the genus Phleum, which consists of 17 species of annual and perennial grasses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Timothy_grass.jpg/330px-Timothy_grass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timothy_(grass)"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Poaceae._-_Phleum_pratense.JPG/250px-Poaceae._-_Phleum_pratense.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Poaceae._-_Phleum_pratense.JPG/500px-Poaceae._-_Phleum_pratense.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Poaceae._-_Phleum_pratense.JPG/250px-Poaceae._-_Phleum_pratense.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu